  "body": "@foolip suggested filing here. I'm seeking a way of switching the burden of Captions/Subtitles verification from the serverside via requiring TRACK be CORS-enabled, to the clientside via the integrity attribute.\n\nAllowing this override (falling back to CORS-enabled requirement if there's no integrity attribute on TRACK) would ease the adoption of accessibility in circumstances where third party servers hosting .vtt files are not CORS configurable by the web author.\n\nI see this as something to introduce as TRACK allows the integrity attribute in future according to the note at\nhttps://w3c.github.io/webappsec-subresource-integrity/#verification-of-html-document-subresources\n\"A future revision of this specification is likely to include integrity support for all possible subresources, i.e., a, audio, embed, iframe, img, link, object, script, source, track, and video elements.\"\n",
